    "rationale": "No such rule exists."
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "content": "It was chosen to make storage devices look bigger",
    "rationale": "Using 1024 actually makes a device's capacity look smaller."
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "content": "Each byte has 1024 bits",
    "rationale": "A byte has 8 bits."
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "content": "Computers work in binary and 1024 is $2^{10}$",
    "correct": true,
    "rationale": "Correct: 1024 is the power of 2 closest to 1000."
   }
  ],
  "explanation": "Memory sizes come in powers of 2. $2^{10} = 1024$ is close to a thousand, so it became the step between units.",
